            "video_2": ""
          }
        },
        "entry_nJrbj4": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "Is it possible to cut my grass too short?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Grass that is cut too short, too often, loses the ability to regenerate the energy it needs to thrive overtime. It can also remove moisture from the soil too rapidly in the summer months. This scorches the grass and contributes to brown patches. A simple solution to prevent this from happening to your lawn, is to raise the cutting height of your mower.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
            "collection": "",
            "collection_products_per_page": 8,
            "products": [],
            "image_loading": "",
            "video_1": "",
            "video_2": ""
          }
        },
        "entry_dT9cR9": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "Why should I leave my grass longer?",
            "text": "<p>Longer grass looks lusher, greener, is more able to out-compete moss and weeds, and will be less stressed and prone to drying out in the summer months.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
            "collection": "",
